issue_context.body:
When using spi_buf_set's it will stop processing spi_buf's at the first occurrence of a buf with length 0 even if there are remanining spi_buf's listed after.

**To Reproduce**

Steps to reproduce the behavior:
```
      struct spi_buf tx_buf_data[] = {{
                                        .buf = bufA,
                                        .len = 10,
                                      },
                                      {
                                        .buf = bufB,
                                        .len = 0,
                                      },
                                      {
                                        .buf = bufC,
                                        .len = 1,
                                      }};
      struct spi_buf_set tx_bufs = {
        .buffers = tx_buf_data,
        .count = ARRAY_SIZE(tx_buf_data),
      };
      spi_write(spi_dev, spi_cfg, &tx_bufs);
```
results in only bufA being sent.
```
      struct spi_buf tx_buf_data[] = {{
                                        .buf = bufA,
                                        .len = 10,
                                      },
                                      {
                                        .buf = bufB,
                                        .len = 1,
                                      },
                                      {
                                        .buf = bufC,
                                        .len = 1,
                                      }};
      struct spi_buf_set tx_bufs = {
        .buffers = tx_buf_data,
        .count = ARRAY_SIZE(tx_buf_data),
      };
      spi_write(spi_dev, spi_cfg, &tx_bufs);
```
results in all 3 buffers being sent.


**Expected behavior**
That all buffers listed in the array will be processed or that the documentation be updated to indicate that a 0 length buffer will stop transmitting any following buffers.

**Impact**
Spent quite a few hours figuring out what was happening.

**Logs and console output**
If applicable, add console logs or other types of debug information
e.g Wireshark capture or Logic analyzer capture (upload in zip archive).
copy-and-paste text and put a code fence (\`\`\`) before and after, to help
explain the issue. (if unable to obtain text log, add a screenshot)

**Environment (please complete the following information):**
 - OS: Linux
 - Toolchain Zephyr SDK 0.1.31
 - Zephyr v2.6.0 (79a6c07536)
 - Target is a nrf52832

**Additional context**
Having the possibility to have 0 byte buffers listed in a spi_buf is quite useful when crafting dynamic messages without having to manually concat the different buffers.
